#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063865 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965ed6b0-0351-5fca-882d-0be68d74d9a6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/id #uuid "2a557e49-5a6c-56c1-9eb8-31e4690b08c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-13202" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x) = \\dfrac{e^{\\left\\lfloor x+2 \\right\\rfloor}}{2x+1}$ at $x = 0.75.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊0.75+2⌋}}{2(0.75)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor 2.75\\right\\rfloor = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2.5} \\\\  & =2.955\\,62… \\\\  & ≈2.96,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063866 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23654a6-05a8-5f59-84a7-2d7a2f758cb1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/id #uuid "44ea15c4-a9d9-529c-ac14-84ba39087e69" :question/math-academy-id "e-13203" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x) = \\left \\lceil e^{6x-5} \\right \\rceil$ at $x = 1.25.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 1.25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.25) & =⌈{e}^{6(1.25)-5}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈{e}^{7.5-5}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈{e}^{2.5}⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left \\lceil e^{2.5} \\right \\rceil = \\left \\lceil 12.182\\,49 \\ldots \\right \\rceil = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.25) & =⌈{e}^{2.5}⌉ \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064025 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eacf715f-6da8-5173-af22-bce603dc83b8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7fbd1a8c-bdd6-5d03-9b3a-69ed01962b1d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6017" :question/problem "If $f(x)=2x+\\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{x}{5} \\right\\rfloor,$ then what is the value of $f(-0.5)?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =2\\cdot (-0.5)+⌊\\frac{-0.5}{5}⌋ \\\\  & =-1+⌊-0.1⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-0.1⌋=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =-1+⌊-0.1⌋ \\\\  & =-1+(-1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45647b2d-10ce-521f-8601-123c659e15f5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9f99283e-05ca-5dd5-97dd-3f872d84f38e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6022" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=(\\lceil 6x-3 \\rceil -2)^3$ at $x=0.4.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =(⌈6(0.4)-3⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(⌈2.4-3⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(⌈-0.6⌉-2)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\lceil -0.6 \\rceil = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =(⌈-0.6⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(-2)^{3} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eacf715f-6da8-5173-af22-bce603dc83b8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2b6a198-eeda-5869-b789-4db047d408d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2b6a198-eeda-5869-b789-4db047d408d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295433} :answer-field/id #uuid "d01329be-979f-589c-8dde-5aefe42cefd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac6958ce-a9fb-557c-a433-b9677624c69e" :question/math-academy-id "q-181718" :question/problem "If $f(x)=⌊3x+2⌋+2,$ then $f(0.5)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.5) & =⌊3(0.5)+2⌋+2 \\\\  & =⌊1.5+2⌋+2 \\\\  & =⌊3.5⌋+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊3.5⌋=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.5) & =⌊3.5⌋+2 \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eacf715f-6da8-5173-af22-bce603dc83b8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f32e49d-d29c-56ad-a9af-de96706bb03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f32e49d-d29c-56ad-a9af-de96706bb03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295436} :answer-field/id #uuid "acf6649a-c157-50da-b9fe-aa1f87808dc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90ade7e1-ff2b-56b2-a925-bd8858c175d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182037" :question/problem "$⌊-9.86⌋=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-9.86⌋=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eacf715f-6da8-5173-af22-bce603dc83b8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140ce5fe-8e8c-5344-b4a2-a9e2aeabb624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "140ce5fe-8e8c-5344-b4a2-a9e2aeabb624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295439} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ab7428-ce9a-5c36-8421-36dae09829e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aac6630f-148b-5958-aa29-0e213785f361" :question/math-academy-id "q-182039" :question/problem "$⌊-5⌋=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-5⌋=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eacf715f-6da8-5173-af22-bce603dc83b8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2398f20-ac07-5402-a255-4506253ecf75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295442} {:answer/id #uuid "835dd112-fb64-5105-8dfd-a43ed625230a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2398f20-ac07-5402-a255-4506253ecf75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295442} :answer-field/id #uuid "b152975e-ce4e-5ff8-8d08-4d635d203354" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0a91aa5-cc4f-5b7d-9737-e4509fc64137" :question/math-academy-id "q-182041" :question/problem "$⌊-42⌋=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-42⌋=-42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eacf715f-6da8-5173-af22-bce603dc83b8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "467d286b-9bb8-5c25-a117-4f2c053d12db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295446} {:answer/id #uuid "f0eb84aa-cfbc-57a1-92ec-6cf3193723bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0eb84aa-cfbc-57a1-92ec-6cf3193723bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295447} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4bbeeb-4e11-59eb-9bad-cb73a8aac836" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e81b0fc8-b33f-524c-bb48-45623c8f9252" :question/math-academy-id "q-182042" :question/problem "If $f(x)=⌊-3x+1⌋+6,$ then $f(1.5)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & =⌊-3(1.5)+1⌋+6 \\\\  & =⌊-4.5+1⌋+6 \\\\  & =⌊-3.5⌋+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-3.5⌋=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & =⌊-3.5⌋+6 \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45647b2d-10ce-521f-8601-123c659e15f5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df3a5280-6bab-51d4-9cf0-8a6ba5ac1416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295450} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4c41dc-4b35-5546-9e6f-323272cbfcb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf4c41dc-4b35-5546-9e6f-323272cbfcb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295451} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd065972-58c0-5656-8698-edb1ce260139" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd886541-a814-50ac-8fd8-5e60159fbe22" :question/math-academy-id "q-182044" :question/problem "$⌈\\pi ⌉=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈\\pi ⌉=⌈3.14…⌉=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45647b2d-10ce-521f-8601-123c659e15f5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b834d584-af78-593c-8b67-2f96e3c394a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295454} {:answer/id #uuid "86d9b07c-3f4f-555c-8b9a-1a53a8ab5167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b834d584-af78-593c-8b67-2f96e3c394a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295454} :answer-field/id #uuid "55313bb4-4bdd-519a-8e3e-9cc7736791ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e6227d8-c2f7-5d6f-8ee1-b2d27a599dfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-182046" :question/problem "$⌈-\\frac{3}{2}⌉=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈-\\frac{3}{2}⌉=⌈-1.5⌉=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45647b2d-10ce-521f-8601-123c659e15f5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d71187b-fb3b-5244-9bd5-71aa6c16f3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d71187b-fb3b-5244-9bd5-71aa6c16f3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295458} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41e77a7-818b-57b4-acc1-18f985b4e3a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67b1fa22-4477-5abe-94f8-aac30960d629" :question/math-academy-id "q-182048" :question/problem "$⌈9⌉=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈9⌉=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45647b2d-10ce-521f-8601-123c659e15f5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1c0f6a0-3e9c-51b7-b4b8-65ffdd6b8798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1c0f6a0-3e9c-51b7-b4b8-65ffdd6b8798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295461} :answer-field/id #uuid "35056a86-f7c5-5590-a03a-2ba10fbfc194" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5fa86eb-ebe1-530d-95bd-205a43e37cc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-182051" :question/problem "If $f(x)=⌈3x-4⌉+2,$ then $f(0.5)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.5) & =⌈3(0.5)-4⌉+2 \\\\  & =⌈1.5-4⌉+2 \\\\  & =⌈-2.5⌉+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈-2.5⌉=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.5) & =⌈-2.5⌉+2 \\\\  & =-2+2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45647b2d-10ce-521f-8601-123c659e15f5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e0579d-1626-54b5-927d-57634bdeb294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46e0579d-1626-54b5-927d-57634bdeb294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295464} :answer-field/id #uuid "66803249-82d8-5333-8e41-2d21e7851d24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a1629051-0c68-504b-b401-aee527c2fb14" :question/math-academy-id "q-182053" :question/problem "If $f(x)=3-⌈1+5x⌉,$ then $f(1.6)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.6) & =3-⌈1+5(1.6)⌉ \\\\  & =3-⌈1+8⌉ \\\\  & =3-⌈9⌉\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈9⌉=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.6) & =3-⌈9⌉ \\\\  & =3-9 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965ed6b0-0351-5fca-882d-0be68d74d9a6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5adb4f0b-6913-5199-b8de-80d783ea2934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295467} {:answer/id #uuid "73f99cdc-80ed-50d1-bc8e-ce7e51a5bd5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295468} {:answer/id #uuid "2ef99386-6300-53b5-aea7-9de658cb82b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295469} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba7ad7e-ff53-52ee-b84c-6400a071ed7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295470} {:answer/id #uuid "38249d8a-83c1-5f28-b0fe-10afba0d1658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ef99386-6300-53b5-aea7-9de658cb82b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295469} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7808bbc-37d0-5acc-a48f-010d462e5695" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4dd2e6d-cdae-54ae-bfed-e87b36f18905" :question/math-academy-id "q-182088" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=x⌊{e}^{x+1}⌋$ at $x=0.75.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =0.75⌊{e}^{0.75+1}⌋ \\\\  & =0.75⌊{e}^{1.75}⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊{e}^{1.75}⌋=⌊5.754\\,60…⌋=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =0.75⌊{e}^{1.75}⌋ \\\\  & =0.75(5) \\\\  & =3.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965ed6b0-0351-5fca-882d-0be68d74d9a6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd55f5f8-35be-52f0-8d3c-4646b1a4c78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061338} {:answer/id #uuid "cf707768-3371-5273-b9f1-bece29eabef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061339} {:answer/id #uuid "ff94b281-5e61-590f-a5f2-80142eeaf8ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061340} {:answer/id #uuid "191d474f-db13-5ecf-a170-9415a33af674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061341} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4d756c-23bd-5c6b-9d61-1877dc0c5ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf707768-3371-5273-b9f1-bece29eabef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061339} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac1da660-38bb-5d17-a2f6-55d6ba10a58d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8ab2d9f9-4d40-5fad-9c33-9145c56d8fdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-182107" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)⌋$ at $x=11.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(11) & =⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡(11+2)⌋ \\\\  & =⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡13⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡13⌋=⌊2.564\\,94…⌋=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(11) & =⌊\\operatorname{ln}⁡13⌋ \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965ed6b0-0351-5fca-882d-0be68d74d9a6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3971bd7-3b75-54fe-885b-7db93f8735fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295474} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ad2a84-4bf2-5405-bdc5-1b1f75fa712a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295475} {:answer/id #uuid "b683540f-e748-5025-a685-fce0477e864c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295476} {:answer/id #uuid "9b07c118-da2a-5e3c-82f0-6f5550f4f0ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295477} {:answer/id #uuid "cc036467-e70e-5821-a4ac-8d40439be2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc036467-e70e-5821-a4ac-8d40439be2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295478} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dbd9d96-e46b-570c-8d77-3c5449244156" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9ea7fc9-051a-5733-a82a-d730d859f0a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-182108" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=x⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡(8x+1)+1⌋$ at $x=3.5.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=3.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.5) & =3.5⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡(8\\cdot 3.5+1)+1⌋ \\\\  & =3.5⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡29+1⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡29+1⌋=⌊2.462\\,39…⌋=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.5) & =3.5⌊\\operatorname{log}⁡29+1⌋ \\\\  & =3.5(2) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23654a6-05a8-5f59-84a7-2d7a2f758cb1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfadc4df-cde6-5657-9a14-675a41a9e304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295481} {:answer/id #uuid "26afa49b-3b25-595b-b7b2-92b2f7405f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295482} {:answer/id #uuid "4faefbcb-ba18-5fff-85a4-e25c43466d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295483} {:answer/id #uuid "7b150086-a3f1-51f0-8393-8e650cc47b70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295484} {:answer/id #uuid "40997390-7c02-550b-ba0d-2f0eb2ee2879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40997390-7c02-550b-ba0d-2f0eb2ee2879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295485} :answer-field/id #uuid "9120a038-c124-5629-9903-c908ad1b5cea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dbe56da-f3e7-5393-952c-9008352b830c" :question/math-academy-id "q-182121" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=⌈x{e}^{x}⌉$ at $x=2.1.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=2.1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.1) & =⌈2.1{e}^{2.1}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈17.148\\,95…⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈17.148\\,95…⌉=18.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.1) & =⌈17.148\\,95…⌉ \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23654a6-05a8-5f59-84a7-2d7a2f758cb1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cd1a49a-2a1b-5e49-a9fc-ba27e5501bf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295488} {:answer/id #uuid "db2b6f68-8d73-57b8-8c1f-19a4d9b79139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295489} {:answer/id #uuid "c09b9f72-bd9e-5b01-aaf3-f9f0ee05010e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295490} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4489a1-fb56-5158-8e0d-86097a60ea62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295491} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf6ce24-904a-5a9b-a98e-bdb732c3e4f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09b9f72-bd9e-5b01-aaf3-f9f0ee05010e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295490} :answer-field/id #uuid "01db70a1-1bcd-5e41-b5cb-16581b1e271a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6e3026d-af3b-5f5b-ad7f-d447198790e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-182123" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{{3}^{⌈5x-2⌉}}{x}$ at $x=0.7.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.7) & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈5(0.7)-2⌉}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈3.5-2⌉}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈1.5⌉}}{0.7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈1.5⌉=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.7) & =\\frac{{3}^{⌈1.5⌉}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{0.7} \\\\  & =12.857\\,14… \\\\  & ≈12.86,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23654a6-05a8-5f59-84a7-2d7a2f758cb1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "601dec4e-d7db-5e3d-9778-148be85f3cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295495} {:answer/id #uuid "6459f238-bd94-5963-acb0-1210034a3b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295496} {:answer/id #uuid "036c76ae-c572-5b00-8a60-8490ae42b4b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295497} {:answer/id #uuid "a324c68f-a2f1-5992-96d9-17bdd9833f0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295498} {:answer/id #uuid "ed550664-600d-5646-b8ab-a58966cc7909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "036c76ae-c572-5b00-8a60-8490ae42b4b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295497} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf8e888-5b56-553d-bffb-c1a01c123d08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1fb79fd6-4849-5195-937b-1bbd8175a75b" :question/math-academy-id "q-182127" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}+1)⌉$ at $x=-2.3.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-2.3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.3) & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((-2.3)^{4}+1)⌉ \\\\  & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(27.984\\,1+1)⌉ \\\\  & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28.984\\,1)⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28.984\\,1)⌉=⌈-3.366\\,74…⌉=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.3) & =⌈-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28.984\\,1)⌉ \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23654a6-05a8-5f59-84a7-2d7a2f758cb1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e34ada55-c41c-5394-905f-27c6663fe0a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295502} {:answer/id #uuid "222fcda2-610c-5a0e-a953-44e272839c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295503} {:answer/id #uuid "4840d798-4e03-568d-b01c-c65fbfe9f04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295504} {:answer/id #uuid "d343f6ca-f897-5dd5-9e69-365f7ec1f624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295505} {:answer/id #uuid "eb0581c8-342b-56b3-9801-1f30e53aa675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d343f6ca-f897-5dd5-9e69-365f7ec1f624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295505} :answer-field/id #uuid "33258313-84f3-551f-9400-b6c546c2f031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b51b28f-291f-569a-843c-85e81062784a" :question/math-academy-id "q-182129" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=⌈x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4)⌉$ at $x=5.7.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=5.7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5.7) & =⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5.7-4)⌉ \\\\  & =⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.7)⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.7)⌉=⌈3.024\\,58……⌉=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5.7) & =⌈5.7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.7)⌉ \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23654a6-05a8-5f59-84a7-2d7a2f758cb1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Ceiling Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5570649e-4cab-574a-b340-30e5bc5f019b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295509} {:answer/id #uuid "9b078fde-fe00-5f50-9a80-42630b795ab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295510} {:answer/id #uuid "63a48602-f8a1-506e-9cd1-b35cabbe4dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295511} {:answer/id #uuid "e26bc628-18e1-595c-b029-44eebc2ef2da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295512} {:answer/id #uuid "458bc474-7549-543e-a6f3-6e8850d62ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b078fde-fe00-5f50-9a80-42630b795ab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295510} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c51fbb6-d490-5fa8-bc5c-3e6da74168b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e1fafe8d-6a16-5b92-b881-e5a7bb62101b" :question/math-academy-id "q-182130" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=x+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡(8x+1)⌉$ at $x=9.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡(8\\cdot 9+1)⌉ \\\\  & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡(72+1)⌉ \\\\  & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡73⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡73⌉=⌈1.863\\,32…⌉=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =9+⌈\\operatorname{log}⁡73⌉ \\\\  & =9+2 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965ed6b0-0351-5fca-882d-0be68d74d9a6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63cda2b9-c052-5152-9d54-e14e12e4bd36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295516} {:answer/id #uuid "4786b28d-8dc8-5724-8f32-772b58473572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295517} {:answer/id #uuid "90e5c532-5fdc-5122-a11f-641965a1c9f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295518} {:answer/id #uuid "5ccc5f5a-7f40-57fd-82bf-d35e19873058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295519} {:answer/id #uuid "906e0699-0465-564d-94f8-193217c4ff33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13.39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ccc5f5a-7f40-57fd-82bf-d35e19873058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295519} :answer-field/id #uuid "f915839c-79f9-578c-a9c8-9160e7f83f65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1348e25a-c183-5e77-8176-6c3e08e34417" :question/math-academy-id "q-41915" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{⌊1-x⌋}}{x}$ at $x=-1.5.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.5) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊1-(-1.5)⌋}}{(-1.5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{⌊1+1.5⌋}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.5⌋}}{1.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊2.5⌋=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.5) & =-\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.5⌋}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-4.926\\,03… \\\\  & ≈-4.93,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965ed6b0-0351-5fca-882d-0be68d74d9a6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Floor Function in More Complex Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78651ca8-50d6-5cab-9999-ef1162f5b12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295523} {:answer/id #uuid "600cd1ee-a68f-57c0-9dfc-e2da236b7cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295524} {:answer/id #uuid "d7681b98-c033-598d-acc0-95e954dfc849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295525} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a412ff-d470-5e4e-952a-83950905ef76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295526} {:answer/id #uuid "1aaaf80c-485c-5d83-9fce-4a0a4f39e3e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "600cd1ee-a68f-57c0-9dfc-e2da236b7cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295524} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ff1fa9d-da68-5eb9-b035-f2ab8983bbd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e7459a5-252e-5299-bd7b-331528e5c9ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-41916" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{⌊{x}^{3}⌋}{{x}^{2}}$ at $x=-2.5.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-2.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.5) & =\\frac{⌊(-2.5)^{3}⌋}{(-2.5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⌊-15.625⌋}{6.25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊-15.625⌋=-16.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.5) & =\\frac{⌊-15.625⌋}{6.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-16)}{6.25} \\\\  & =-2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
